# Allowlist for scripts/scan-secrets.mjs (the repository's own secret scanner).
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#   <path-glob> [rules=rule-a,rule-b]  # <justification: required, at least 8 characters>
#
# Rules of the road:
#   - Every entry MUST explain why the match is not a real credential; the scanner refuses to run
#     with an entry that has no justification.
#   - Prefer an inline `allow` marker (see CONTRIBUTING.md) for a single line; use this file only
#     for whole files or directories.
#   - Scope entries to specific rules wherever possible so that unrelated detections stay active.
#   - Never allow-list a real credential. Rotate it instead.

synthetic-data/** rules=aws-access-key-id,aws-secret-access-key,github-token,slack-token,slack-webhook,stripe-secret-key,google-api-key,npm-token,azure-storage-account-key,azure-shared-access-key,azure-sas-token,azure-ad-client-secret,appinsights-instrumentation-key,jwt,credential-in-url,generic-secret-assignment  # synthetic case bundles carry generated, secret-shaped canary strings on purpose to exercise FR-ING-04 redaction; private-key and key-file rules stay enforced
packages/security/test/redaction-property.test.ts rules=private-key  # redactor linear-time tests feed PEM header-only strings (no base64 key material) as hostile input; one file and one rule only
